// Label propagation, on the merge series: the case that needs it.
//
// The series is frames/merge_<t>.png, drawn in frames/draw.py with the
// expected result. What at frame 2 descends from lesion 1 of frame 0 is, by
// propagation through the merged lesion of frame 1, the whole lesion of frame
// 2; and so does what descends from lesion 2. Their intersection is the merged
// lesion, shifted and all: the merge, seen two frames later, through a frame
// where the region had to be followed by overlap. Expected: the lesion of
// frame 2 (frames/merge-tracked.expected.png).
//
// Under footprint labelling the two regions never overlap, and neither do they
// under the labels of frame 0 alone: both give an empty result. This is the
// case neither initially nor the footprint can pass. The third pass is the
// semantics written out: eq(lcc(lesion at 0), l), then through with the lesion
// at 1, then at 2, for each label, and their and.
let video = load("merge")
let lesion = gt(intensity(frame(video,n)),127)
save "merge-tracked" diamond(diamond(and(tracked(lesion,1),tracked(lesion,2))))
